// Plan stage R0z Z9c-C (part 4, removed in review round 1: code of a caller holds `r` across the run of the closure of `mid`; f only reads; the program keeps `NESTED_TASK_RUN`, the rule of main); the clean twin.
fn mid(g: fn(fn()), f: fn()) / async { g(|| scope { s => s.spawn(f); () }) }
fn main() / async {
    let w = [1]
    mid(|x| { let r = &w[0]; x(); print(r) }, || print(w.len()))
}
